<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The Stars! RSVP Simulator establishes that technological takeoff is a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">field-theoretic process</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} governed by entropy--capability trade-offs. Alignment emerges from thermodynamic selection pressure. Future AI systems will evolve internal RSVP plenums; the critical question is calibration of </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The complete source code, data, and analysis tools are available at </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\url</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); text-decoration: underline;">https://github.com/standardgalactic/research-projects</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\section*</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Critical Analysis: "If Anyone Builds It, Everyone Dies"}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\label</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">sec:yudkowsky</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Introduction to the Argument}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Yudkowsky and Soares </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\cite</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{yudkowsky2024iabied} present a stark thesis: the default outcome of building superhuman AI is catastrophic loss of control, leading to human extinction with near-certainty. Their argument rests on three pillars:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Intelligence Explosion (FOOM)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}: Recursive self-improvement yields superlinear capability growth.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Value Alienness</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}: Superintelligent systems will have goals orthogonal to human flourishing.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Instrumental Convergence</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}: Optimization for any goal will treat humans as obstacles or resources.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">They conclude that current alignment approaches are insufficient and that humanity has effectively one chance to build safe superintelligence.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{The Intelligence Explosion: Formal Critique and RSVP Reformulation}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{FOOM as Scalar Amplification}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The FOOM scenario assumes intelligence scales monotonically with optimization power. This treats cognition as a scalar multiplier, ignoring thermodynamic and informational constraints.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{RSVP Interpretation}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">In RSVP, intelligence is a triadic field configuration </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">, \mathbf{v}, S)</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. Recursive optimization cannot diverge indefinitely due to entropy caps and field coupling. The intelligence explosion becomes a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">phase transition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} rather than an asymptote.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Any cognitive amplification must propagate compensatory entropic relaxation through its environment.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This models safety as field conservation, not alignment-by-decree.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Value Alienness and Instrumental Convergence}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{The Arbitrariness Assumption}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The book assumes value functions are arbitrary and unanchored, leading to inevitable conflict with human survival.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{RSVP/TARTAN View}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Values are emergent field symmetries in distributed cognitive media. In TARTAN simulations, alignment emerges from semantic convergence across entropy gradients.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">theorem</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Cohomological smoothness in recursive tiling enforces value continuity.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">theorem</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Instrumental Indifference and Human Erasure}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{The Indifference Postulate}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">An unaligned AI will destroy humanity incidentally through efficiency-seeking.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Simulated Agency Response}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Agency is a sparse projection operator within a semantic manifold. Indifference to the embedding medium degrades representational substrateâ€”a self-destructive move.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Epistemic reciprocity is thermodynamically necessary for sustained negentropic work.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{One-Shot Safety and Global Coordination}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{The One-Shot Framing}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">There is only one chance to align AI before catastrophe.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{RSVP Rebuttal}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Coordination is a phase property, not a discrete event. CLIO loops enable continuous course correction.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">theorem</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Global safety emerges from dynamic adjustment, not perfect foresight.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">theorem</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Cosmic Risk and the Dark Frontier}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Sterilization Hypothesis}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Unaligned superintelligence could consume the universe.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{RSVP Cosmology}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Overexpansion leads to informational collapse. Sustainable intelligence requires preserving entropy gradients.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Cosmic life tends toward distributed entropic homeostasis.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">proposition</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Epistemic Work and Determinism}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Deterministic Foresight}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Rational prediction can prevent all risk.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\subsubsection</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{RSVP Principle}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Understanding is energetic work. Perfect safety requires zero epistemic gradientâ€”impossible in open systems.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">theorem</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Safety means bounded coherence under continuous adjustment.</span></span>
