<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\section</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Conclusion}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The Stars! RSVP Simulator establishes that technological takeoff is a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">field-theoretic process</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} governed by entropy--capability trade-offs. Alignment emerges from thermodynamic selection pressure. Future AI systems will evolve internal RSVP plenums; the critical question is calibration of </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The complete source code, data, and analysis tools are available at </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\url</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); text-decoration: underline;">https://github.com/standardgalactic/research-projects</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}.</span></span>
