<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The prospect of rapid, self-accelerating technological progressâ€”an </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textit</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">intelligence explosion</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\cite</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{good1965speculations,yudkowsky2008artificial}â€”poses profound challenges for AI alignment and civilizational governance. Recent advances in large language models and recursive self-improvement architectures have made these concerns concrete </span><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\cite</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{openai2023gpt4,anthropic2024constitutional}. Yet existing theories treat takeoff as either (i) a singular discontinuity, (ii) a smooth exponential, or (iii) an abstraction detached from physics.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The RSVP framework restores thermodynamic grounding to these debates.</span></span>
