(iv) define an empirical safety bound </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\dot{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Sigma</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}_{\text{crit}}=</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">2.1</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\pm</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0.4</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> nats/generation; and (v) recast Yudkowskyâ€“Soares doomsday premises as limiting cases </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\to</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">. We present operational mappings from RSVP variables to observable quantities (compute, power, inference entropy), add sensitivity and convergence analyses, and provide a conservative alignment theorem with explicit assumptions. We conclude with governance instruments implementable today.</span></span>
