<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">Doomsday theses by Yudkowsky and Yampolski presuppose a closed-world model of optimization: that intelligence, given sufficient gradient ascent on utility, converges to domination. Yet civilization operates as an \emph{open, non-equilibrium field} where agency disperses faster than it concentrates. Their error is to treat agency as scalar, not vectorial.</span></span>
