<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">We fit the logistic form</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\[</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\Phi</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">(t) = \frac{</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">1</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">}{</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">1</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> + e^{-r(t-t_</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">)}},</span></span>
